  "reason": "The strongest completed result is RNA-only PCA with multiprofile avgpool (accuracy 0.591, F1 0.573), and it clearly outperforms both singleprofile PCA and transformer aggregation for PCA. The key uncertainty is whether the RNA representation itself can be improved beyond PCA while preserving this promising profile/aggregation setting. config_005 keeps multiprofile avgpool fixed and changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200, isolating the effect of representation. This is a focused extension of the current best RNA direction, has a plausible chance of improving validation accuracy, and will inform whether scvi-based configurations are worth testing later without changing multiple design choices at once."
